# EphCore — Getting Started

```elixir
Mix.install(
  [
    {:eph_core, path: Path.join(__DIR__, "..")},
    {:kino, "~> 0.14"}
  ],
  config: [
    eph_core: [
      # Planetary DE440s only. Avoid config_path: :eph_core here — that loads
      # config.exs asteroid kernels before SPK.Server starts.
      kernel_base_dir: Path.expand("../priv", __DIR__),
      spk_kernels: ["de440s.bsp"]
    ]
  ]
)

Logger.configure(level: :warning)
```

## Overview

Interactive lab for the pure-Elixir ephemeris engine. Change the observer, call
`observe/4`, and compare geometric vs apparent frames without leaving the browser.
This file is the front door: start here for one working result, then choose the
mechanics path or the application path below.

**How to open:** Install [Livebook](https://livebook.dev/), open this `.livemd`,
evaluate the setup cell. Kernels must already be under `eph_core/priv/ephemeris/`
(run `mix eph.download_kernels` in the repo first; the setup cell will not start without baseline files).

## Tour paths

The notebooks are split into two tracks.

### 01 — Observe pipeline

This path answers: if you call `observe/4`, what happens between the inputs and
the celestial-sphere output?

Use this path as the public-surface tour. The notebooks should call EphCore
functions wherever possible; they should not teach readers to recreate core
library behavior in notebook-local code.

